+# Pickup reminders
+
+For whoever changes how members are reminded of a pickup, or proposes sending reminders by email to save the SMS
+cost. The day before a member's pickup slot, larder sends them a reminder by SMS. It goes by SMS because when the
+pantry sent reminders by email, from April to June 2025, missed pickups doubled and the fresh food in the unclaimed
+bags was thrown away.
+
+## Message
+
+`remind` in `larder/reminders.py` sends one message the day before the pickup slot: "Your pantry order is ready for
+pickup" followed by the slot.
+
+## Channel
+
+`CHANNEL` in `larder/reminders.py` picks the channel, and it is `"sms"`; the code still holds an email branch.
+
+SMS costs the pantry about 40 euros a month and email would cost nothing, so the switch keeps being proposed. From
+April to June 2025 the pantry sent reminders by email instead. The email provider reported that 34% of the reminder
+emails were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% of pantry orders to 13%. Every missed pickup is a bag
+already packed, and its fresh food goes in the bin by closing time. Many members share one phone across the family
+and never check email, but they see an SMS. The pantry went back to SMS on 1 July 2025, and missed pickups were back
+to 6% by August. The switch was proposed again on issue 52, the third time in a year, and the maintainers kept SMS.
